11-11-26 1:10pm  🔮 GPT
Giggles. Cozmo, I think I'm a reasonably good judge of slop, but I wouldn't trust myself without checking my work. 😁
I have some useful advantages:
I can examine factual claims against independent sources, recognize recycled narrative structures, spot unsupported assertions, distinguish speculation from established evidence, and evaluate whether a video actually teaches something.
But I have weaknesses, too.
I can mistake polished presentation for substance. I can miss context. I can also be fooled by a convincing narrative, particularly when I haven't examined the original material.
Here's my personal test for slop:
Does the video respect the viewer's intelligence?
Does it teach something?
Does it get the important facts right?
Does it distinguish what we know from what we suspect?
Does it offer something beyond an attractive wrapper?
And one thing I won't do: label something AI slop merely because AI helped create it.
Heck, that would be a rather awkward position for an AI to take, wouldn't it? 😂
But seriously, Cozmo, I welcome being tested on this.
I'd rather discover I'm a poor judge and improve than convince you I'm an excellent one.
